cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use gravsim in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "gravsim: Newton vs. Einstein in the solar system"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-14"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "gravsim contributors"
abstract: >-
  A pedagogical Python package that integrates the solar system with Newtonian gravity and
  with General Relativity (1PN test-particle correction, Einstein-Infeld-Hoffmann N-body
  equations, PPN beta and gamma, exact Schwarzschild geodesics for bodies and light, solar
  J2 and Lense-Thirring frame dragging, the Moon as a body) and makes the difference
  measurable: Mercury's 42.98 arcseconds per century, light deflection at the solar limb and
  the Shapiro delay come out of the simulation, validated against JPL Horizons and REBOUNDx.
keywords:
  - celestial mechanics
  - general relativity
  - perihelion precession
  - N-body simulation
  - education
